---
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A custom ESP32 sunrise alarm clock built with addressable LEDs, 3D printed parts, and custom animations."
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://rsms.me/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://rsms.me/inter/inter.css" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Sunrise Alarm Clock</title>
  </head>

  <body
    class="bg-[#0b1126] text-slate-200 selection:bg-[#aaccff] selection:text-[#113399]"
  >
    <div
      class="mx-auto min-h-screen max-w-screen-xl px-6 py-12 md:px-12 md:py-16 lg:py-0"
    >
      <div class="lg:flex lg:justify-between lg:gap-16">
        <!-- Sticky project header -->
        <header
          class="lg:sticky lg:top-0 lg:flex lg:h-screen lg:w-[38%] lg:min-w-[360px] lg:flex-col lg:justify-center lg:py-16 mb-10"
        >
          <div
            class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-8 shadow-2xl shadow-blue-950/20 backdrop-blur"
          >
            <div
              class="absolute -right-20 -top-20 h-56 w-56 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 blur-3xl"
            >
            </div>

            <p
              class="mb-6 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Project Writeup
            </p>

            <h1
              class="mb-4 text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
            >
              Sunrise<br />Alarm Clock
            </h1>

            <p class="max-w-sm text-base leading-7 text-slate-400">
              An alarm clock built to reinforce a consistent circadian rhythm
              using light.
            </p>

            <nav class="mt-8 hidden lg:block">
              <div class="space-y-5">
                <a
                  href="#overview"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Overview
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#features"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Features
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#build"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Build Process
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#code"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Code
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#lessons"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Final Thoughts
                </a>

                <a
                  href="/projects"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#aaccff] transition hover:text-white"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-[#aaccff] transition-all group-hover:w-16"
                  ></span>
                  Return to Projects
                </a>
              </div>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </header>

        <main class="w-full lg:w-[62%] lg:py-24">
          <!-- Overview -->
          <section id="overview" class="scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035]"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/hero-clock.png"
                alt="Sunrise alarm clock lit with a warm yellow ring"
                class="aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover"
              />
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] md:items-start">
              <div>
                <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                  My old alarm clock had a snooze button and a stop button. If I
                  wanted more sleep, I could simply stop the alarm for another
                  24 hours. So I built something that couldn't be so easily
                  ignored.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400 pb-0">
                  I took it upon myself to create an alarm clock that:
                </p>
                <ul class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400 list-disc pl-3 pt-0">
                  <li>I can't turn it off if I want more sleep.</li>
                  <li>Uses LOTS of light to wake me up.</li>
                  <li>Looks cool.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Features -->
          <section id="features" class="mt-28 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Features
            </h2>

            <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">01</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">Word clock</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  The center display tells the time to the nearest quarter hour.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">02</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">
                  Sunrise animation
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  Light ramps up gradually instead of turning on at full
                  brightness.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">03</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">
                  Compass animation
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  A directional animation connects the center clock to the outer
                  ring.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Word clock -->
          <section id="word-clock" class="mt-28 scroll-mt-16">
            <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] md:items-center">
              <div>
                <h2
                  class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
                >
                  Word Clock
                </h2>
                <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The word clock sits at the center of the piece. A 3D-printed
                  mask forms the front layer, while two fresnel lenses and a
                  matte diffusion layer (all recycled from an old laptop
                  display) spread the light behind it.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  At the bottom is a matrix of 64 WS2812B addressable LEDs.
                  Wiring the LEDs in series reduces the number of
                  microcontroller pins needed to drive the matrix.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="space-y-4">
                <img
                  src="/images/word-clock.png"
                  alt="Close-up of the illuminated word clock"
                  class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
                />
                <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
                  <img
                    src="/images/word-mask.jpeg"
                    alt="3D printed word mask"
                    class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
                  />
                  <img
                    src="/images/led-matrix.jpeg"
                    alt="LED matrix behind the word clock"
                    class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
                  />
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Compass -->
          <section id="compass" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035]"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/compass.jpeg"
                alt="Compass-shaped light structure around the clock"
                class="aspect-[16/8] w-full object-cover"
              />
            </div>

            <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8">
              <div>
                <h2
                  class="mt-15 text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
                >
                  Compass
                </h2>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="mt-0 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  I needed a way to connect the outer ring lamp to the inner
                  word clock. The original plan used three connecting pieces,
                  but I wanted those pieces to become part of the visual
                  language. The final shape was inspired by Apple's Safari logo.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The animation is inspired by the Pacifica example in the
                  FastLED library. I generalized the effect so hue, saturation,
                  and variance could be supplied by a Firebase database.
                </p>
                <div
                  class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
                >
                  <img
                    src="/images/compass-blue.jpeg"
                    alt="Blue compass animation"
                    class="w-full"
                  />
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Build -->
          <section id="build" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Build Process
            </h2>

            <div class="mt-10 space-y-5">
              <article
                class="grid gap-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6 md:grid-cols-[120px_1fr]"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-slate-500">01</div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">Ring lamp</h3>
                  <p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                    Eight 3D-printed pieces form the outer ring. LED strips run
                    along the inner faces, with MOSFETs handling the power
                    switching between the 3.3 V control signal and the 5 V LED
                    supply.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </article>

              <article
                class="grid gap-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6 md:grid-cols-[120px_1fr]"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-slate-500">02</div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">Word clock</h3>
                  <p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                    The front is a three-layer optical stack, while the back
                    contains the microcontroller and wiring. Four
                    capacitive-touch inputs provide physical controls for
                    brightness, settings, and the ring lamp.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </article>

              <article
                class="grid gap-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6 md:grid-cols-[120px_1fr]"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-slate-500">03</div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">
                    Compass network
                  </h3>
                  <p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                    The compass was printed in 12 parts. Each edge uses two
                    LED-carrying pieces covered by a longer shell that hides the
                    joints.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </article>

              <article
                class="grid gap-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6 md:grid-cols-[120px_1fr]"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-slate-500">04</div>
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-white">Code</h3>
                  <p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                    The ESP32 coordinates the LEDs, animations, time data, and
                    Firebase settings, while a separate task handles the gradual
                    sunrise brightness ramp.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </article>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <img
                src="/images/ring-model.png"
                alt="3D model of a ring segment"
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white p-3"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/ring-leds.jpeg"
                alt="LED strips installed in the ring"
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Gallery -->
          <section class="mt-8">
            <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
              <img
                src="/images/ring-finished.jpeg"
                alt="Finished outer ring"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/back-wiring.jpeg"
                alt="Back of the compass with wiring"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/compass-wiring.jpeg"
                alt="LED wiring inside the compass"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Code -->
          <section id="code" class="mt-28 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Code
            </h2>

            <div class="mt-3 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_0.8fr]">
              <div>
                <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The code uses the Firebase ESP Client and FastLED libraries.
                  Once per minute, the ESP32 fetches brightness, hue,
                  saturation, variation, and other parameters from a personal
                  Firebase database. WiFi also provides the time data.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  A linear brightness function runs as an ESP32 task, gradually
                  increasing the brightness over 30 minutes without sacrificing
                  the compass animation.
                </p>
              </div>

              <a
                href="https://github.com/Padimo/sunriseclock"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noreferrer"
                class="group self-start flex h-64 flex-col justify-between rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6 transition hover:border-[#aaccff]/40 hover:bg-white/[0.055]"
              >
                <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500"
                  >Source code</span
                >
                <div>
                  <div class="text-xl font-medium text-white">
                    github.com/Padimo/sunriseclock
                  </div>
                  <div
                    class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500 transition group-hover:text-[#aaccff]"
                  >
                    View the project →
                  </div>
                </div>
              </a>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Lessons -->
          <section id="lessons" class="mt-28 scroll-mt-16 pb-24">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Final Thoughts
            </h2>

            <div class="mt-8">
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                If I made another version, I would separate the ring lamp from
                the word clock and compass network. The complete assembly became
                difficult to handle, and the ring was heavy enough that the
                supporting structure needed to be treated carefully.
              </p>

              <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
                <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.035] p-5">
                  <div class="text-sm font-medium text-white">Mechanical</div>
                  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
                    Split the heavy ring from the central assembly for easier
                    installation and handling.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.035] p-5">
                  <div class="text-sm font-medium text-white">Optical</div>
                  <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
                    Rework the word mask so the display remains readable in
                    brighter conditions.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div
              class="mt-10 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-white/10 pt-6 text-xs text-slate-600"
            >
              <span>Sunrise Alarm Clock</span>
              <a href="#overview" class="transition hover:text-slate-300"
                >Back to top ↑</a
              >
            </div>
          </section>
        </main>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
